1
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:19,930
Where you gonna go?

2
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,030
South.

3
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,160
What are you gonna do?

4
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,740
Get warm.

5
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:37,300
I was with you at Hardhome.

6
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,380
We saw what's out there.

7
00:02:41,330 --> 00:02:42,810
We know it's coming here.

8
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:45,000
How can you leave us now?

9
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,160
I did everything I could. You know that.

10
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:51,470
- You swore a vow. - Aye, I pledged my life to the Night's Watch.

11
00:02:51,470 --> 00:02:53,450
- I gave my life. - For all nights to come.

12
00:02:53,450 --> 00:02:55,840
They killed me, Edd! My own brothers.

13
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,000
You want me to stay here after that?

14
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:01,020
Riders approaching!

15
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:02,910
Open the gate!

16
00:04:37,490 --> 00:04:38,680
This is good soup.

17
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:44,450
Do you remember those kidney pies Old Nan used to make?

18
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:46,400
With the peas and onions?

19
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:52,340
We never should have left Winterfell.

20
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,850
Don't you wish we could go back to the day we left?

21
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,990
I want to scream at myself, "Don't go, you idiot."

22
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,890
How could we know?

23
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:07,940
I spent a lot of time thinking about what an ass I was to you.

24
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:11,970
I wish I could change everything.

25
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,310
We were children.

26
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,470
I was awful, just admit it.

27
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:19,120
You were occasionally awful.

28
00:05:19,850 --> 00:05:21,520
I'm sure I can't have been great fun.

29
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:24,330
Always sulking in the corner while the rest of you played.

30
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,270
- Can you forgive me? - There's nothing to forgive.

31
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,800
- Forgive me. - All right.

32
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,010
All right, I forgive you.

33
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:49,490
You'd think after thousands of years,

34
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:52,150
the Night's Watch would have learned how to make a good ale.

35
00:05:55,860 --> 00:05:56,990
Where will you go?

36
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:00,050
Where will we go?

37
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,620
If I don't watch over you,

38
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,870
Father's ghost will come back and murder me.

39
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:08,930
Where will we go?

40
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:11,860
I can't stay here, not after what happened.

41
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:13,800
There's only one place we can go.

42
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,260
Home.

43
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,640
Should we tell the Boltons to pack up and leave?

44
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,210
We'll take it back from them.

45
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,920
I don't have an army.

46
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:28,190
How many wildlings did you save?

47
00:06:28,190 --> 00:06:29,880
They didn't come here to serve me.

48
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,580
They owe you their lives.

49
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,390
You think they'll be safe here

50
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:35,160
if Roose Bolton remains Warden of the North?

51
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,270
- Sansa. - Winterfell is our home.

52
00:06:37,850 --> 00:06:41,210
It's ours and Arya's and Bran's and Rickon's.

53
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:43,430
Wherever they are, it belongs to our family.

54
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:44,870
We have to fight for it.

55
00:06:44,870 --> 00:06:46,730
I'm tired of fighting.

56
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,510
It's all I've done since I left home.

57
00:06:52,230 --> 00:06:54,000
I've killed brothers of the Night's Watch.

58
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,740
I've killed wildlings. I've killed men that I admire.

59
00:06:56,740 --> 00:07:00,210
I hanged a boy younger than Bran.

60
00:07:02,850 --> 00:07:07,190
I fought and I lost.

61
00:07:11,290 --> 00:07:14,570
If we don't take back the North, we'll never be safe.

62
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,990
I want you to help me.

63
00:07:19,970 --> 00:07:22,160
But I'll do it myself if I have to.

64
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:26,940
My lady.

65
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,910
Ser Davos.

66
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,150
Will you stay here at Castle Black?

67
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:37,990
I will do as Jon Snow commands.

68
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,920
You serve Jon Snow now?

69
00:07:42,610 --> 00:07:44,360
He's the prince that was promised.

70
00:07:46,350 --> 00:07:48,880
Forgive me, my lady, I thought that was Stannis.

71
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:01,000
What happened down there?

72
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:06,370
There was a battle. Stannis was defeated.

73
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,510
And Shireen?

74
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:12,370
What happened to the princess?

75
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:13,930
I saw what happened.

76
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,960
I saw Stannis' forces defeated in the field.

77
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,770
My lady, I'm Ser Davos Seaworth.

78
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:21,040
We've met before.

79
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:23,930
I was Kingsguard to Renly Baratheon.

80
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,750
Before Renly was assassinated with bloodmagic.

81
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:30,690
That's in the past now.

82
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:33,790
Yes, it's in the past.

83
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,360
It doesn't mean I forget.

84
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,490
Or forgive.

85
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,740
He admitted it, you know.

86
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,870
Who did?

87
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,180
Stannis.

88
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,190
Just before I executed him.

89
00:09:35,370 --> 00:09:37,210
The Defender of the Vale!

90
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:38,490
Uncle Petyr!

91
00:09:46,310 --> 00:09:47,290
My lord.

92
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,000
Come and see.

93
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,450
I missed your name day. Go on.

94
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,060
A falcon!

95
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,350
A gyrfalcon.

96
00:09:57,850 --> 00:09:59,770
The greatest and rarest of birds.

97
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,260
Last time I saw you, Baelish,

98
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:06,380
you told me you were taking Sansa Stark home with you to the Fingers.

99
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:07,610
Indeed I was.

100
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:10,220
And yet not long ago, we received reports

101
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:13,510
that she has been married to Ramsay Bolton in Winterfell.

102
00:10:13,510 --> 00:10:14,530
On our way to the Fingers,

103
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:17,450
we were set upon by a large force of Bolton men.

104
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,660
Seemed to know exactly when we were traveling

105
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,490
and exactly whom we were transporting.

106
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:23,090
Do you take me for a fool?

107
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,070
Tell me, Lord Royce,

108
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:30,120
how many people knew of my travel plans with Sansa Stark?

109
00:10:30,850 --> 00:10:32,830
I shared my intentions with you

110
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:34,490
and no one else.

111
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:38,760
Slander a man in his own home,

112
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:42,830
you might find yourself crossing swords with him.

113
00:10:43,270 --> 00:10:46,860
Your home is the Vale. The Lord of the Vale stands before us.

114
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:49,410
And only his judgment concerns me.

115
00:10:55,910 --> 00:10:57,480
Shall we throw him through the Moon Door?

116
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:05,870
My lord.

117
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:11,780
My lord, I have always been faithful to House Arryn.

118
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:14,820
To your father, to your mother, and now to you.

119
00:11:16,450 --> 00:11:17,820
Do you believe him, Uncle Petyr?

120
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,010
Lord Royce has served the Vale well.

121
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:32,150
He's enjoyed a distinguished military career.

122
00:11:32,950 --> 00:11:35,530
If we could trust his absolute loyalty,

123
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:39,340
he would make a capable commander in the wars to come.

124
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:46,200
You can trust my absolute loyalty, my lord.

125
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,270
I think he deserves one more chance. What do you say?

126
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,460
Fine.

127
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:06,730
I bring good news.

128
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:10,010
My friends in the North tell me Sansa has escaped Winterfell.

129
00:12:10,010 --> 00:12:11,470
I expect she's headed to Castle Black

130
00:12:11,470 --> 00:12:13,630
where her brother serves as Lord Commander.

131
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:18,320
But she won't be safe there, not with the Boltons after her.

132
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,230
She's my cousin.

133
00:12:25,770 --> 00:12:26,550
We should help her.

134
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:28,390
That was my instinct as well.

135
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,750
Our lord has spoken.

136
00:12:32,930 --> 00:12:34,520
Gather the Knights of the Vale.

137
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:37,860
The time has come to join the fray.

138
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:44,460
You invite the enemy into our city?

139
00:12:44,470 --> 00:12:45,400
I did.

140
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:49,050
As a clever man once told me,

141
00:12:49,050 --> 00:12:52,120
"We make peace with our enemies, not our friends."

142
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,470
I don't make peace with the queen's enemies.

143
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:55,780
I kill the queen's enemies.

144
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:57,590
Yes, that's the military approach.

145
00:12:57,590 --> 00:12:59,590
And how has that worked here in Meereen?

146
00:12:59,770 --> 00:13:01,660
I represent the diplomatic approach.

147
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:03,770
Our queen tried to make peace with the Masters

148
00:13:03,770 --> 00:13:05,400
and they tried to murder her.

149
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:09,610
We enter these negotiations with open eyes.

150
00:13:09,610 --> 00:13:12,450
Trust me. My own recent experience with slavery

151
00:13:12,450 --> 00:13:14,380
has taught me the horrors of that institution.

152
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:16,100
How many days were you a slave?

153
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,090
Long enough to know.

154
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:20,830
Not long enough to understand.

155
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:30,410
I bought this dwarf for a single gold honor.

156
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,280
And somehow you've risen

157
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:36,250
to the top of the Great Pyramid of Meereen.

158
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,130
It's most impressive.

159
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:41,100
And now you speak for the Good Masters of Astapor.

160
00:13:41,510 --> 00:13:43,600
Here's to reversals of fortune.

161
00:13:43,690 --> 00:13:45,340
We came here to meet the queen

162
00:13:45,390 --> 00:13:48,190
and instead we're greeted by a dwarf and a eunuch.

163
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:50,010
Let's make this simple, shall we?

164
00:13:50,850 --> 00:13:52,150
Tell me what you want.

165
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:54,230
We want you to leave Slaver's Bay.

166
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:58,800
Take your dragons and your mercenaries and go.

167
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,270
Queen Daenerys won't stay in Meereen forever.

168
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,340
Her path takes her westward.

169
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:05,880
When we last met, I offered her ships

170
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,640
so she could return to Westeros where she belongs.

171
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:09,600
She refused them.

172
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,030
She refused them because hundreds of thousands of men,

173
00:14:12,030 --> 00:14:13,900
women, and children still lived in chains.

174
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:16,510
As they have since the dawn of time.

175
00:14:16,510 --> 00:14:17,580
Not anymore.

176
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:19,320
You think you're a free man now?

177
00:14:19,810 --> 00:14:21,520
You still follow orders.

178
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,070
Just because your master has silver hair and tits

179
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:26,100
doesn't mean she's not a master.

180
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:29,450
Friends, friends, friends, please.

181
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:31,930
There have always been those

182
00:14:31,930 --> 00:14:34,500
with wealth and power and those with nothing.

183
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:35,460
That is the way of the world.

184
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:37,250
I'm not here to change the way of the world.

185
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:39,890
Slavery is the way of our world.

186
00:14:39,890 --> 00:14:43,210
You don't need slaves to make money.

187
00:14:43,730 --> 00:14:46,380
There haven't been slaves in Westeros for hundreds of years

188
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:48,570
and I grew up richer than any of you.

189
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:56,400
But our queen recognizes that she erred by abolishing slavery

190
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,840
without providing a new system to replace it.

191
00:15:00,090 --> 00:15:02,660
So here is the queen's proposal.

192
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:06,280
Slavery will never return to Meereen,

193
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,480
but she will give the other cities of Slaver's Bay

194
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:11,690
time to adjust to the new order.

195
00:15:11,690 --> 00:15:13,070
What does that mean?

196
00:15:13,070 --> 00:15:15,460
Instead of abolishing slavery overnight,

197
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:19,350
we will give you seven years to end the practice.

198
00:15:24,330 --> 00:15:26,580
Slaveholders will be compensated for their losses,

199
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:28,640
of course, at fair prices.

200
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,380
In exchange, you will cut off

201
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:33,080
your support for the Sons of the Harpy.

202
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:34,790
We do not support the Sons of the Harpy.

203
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:38,170
Fine, fine, but you will cut it off all the same.

204
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:41,090
I do hope you accept, my friends.

205
00:15:42,130 --> 00:15:44,070
You will not receive a better offer.

206
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:50,210
Let us sail on the tide of freedom

207
00:15:50,590 --> 00:15:52,530
instead of being drowned by it.

208
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:57,360
And as a parting gift to our honored guests...

209
00:16:06,410 --> 00:16:07,800
Give freedom a chance.

210
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:11,400
See if it doesn't taste every bit as good as what came before.

211
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:34,760
Perhaps I should translate for you.

212
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,390
We speak the Common Tongue.

213
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,040
- Excellent. - You met with the slavers today.

214
00:16:40,530 --> 00:16:41,230
I did.

215
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,620
Our brothers and sisters died fighting this scum.

216
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,270
Now you invite them to our city and drink wine with them.

217
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:52,910
I imagine this room was built

218
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:55,610
so the rulers could intimidate the ruled.

219
00:16:56,770 --> 00:16:59,110
But I am not your ruler.

220
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:02,060
I'm not the Breaker of Chains.

221
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,770
I'm not the Unburnt.

222
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:08,000
And I am certainly not the Mother of Dragons.

223
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,100
You are a stranger here.

224
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:14,040
So why do you represent Meereen in these talks with our enemies?

225
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:16,910
Because our queen chose me as her advisor.

226
00:17:17,910 --> 00:17:19,410
Until she returns from her travels...

227
00:17:19,410 --> 00:17:21,000
When does she return?

228
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,800
Soon. You have my word.

229
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:27,450
We don't know you. We don't trust you. We know Torgo Nudho.

230
00:17:27,450 --> 00:17:29,890
We fight with him against the Masters. We trust him.

231
00:17:29,890 --> 00:17:33,540
And that is exactly why grey Worm took part in these negotiations.

232
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:36,930
As commander of the Unsullied, he knows how to defeat the slavers

233
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:39,230
and he knows when it is time to make peace.

234
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:42,080
You have made peace with the slavers?

235
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,590
We offered terms.

236
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:39,460
- Do not use me for your lies. - Those men respect you.

237
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,860
They respect me because they know who I am.

238
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:43,990
- They know I am loyal. - As do I.

239
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,190
I am loyal to my queen, not you.

240
00:18:46,190 --> 00:18:48,400
If you betray her work, you are my enemy.

241
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:51,470
I am not betraying her work. I am trying to save her city.

242
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:53,850
You promised the slavers they could keep slavery.

243
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:55,050
For a short time.

244
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:58,030
Seven years is not a short time for a slave.

245
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,540
You're right.

246
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:02,170
Slavery is a horror that should be ended at once.

247
00:19:02,170 --> 00:19:04,820
War is a horror that should be ended at once.

248
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,690
I can't do both today.

249
00:19:06,690 --> 00:19:08,370
You are wrong to trust these men.

250
00:19:08,370 --> 00:19:11,980
I don't trust the Masters. I trust their self-interest.

251
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,780
They're trustworthy if they're convinced

252
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,900
that working with me is in their self-interest.

253
00:19:15,910 --> 00:19:18,730
You don't know them. You don't understand them.

254
00:19:18,730 --> 00:19:20,860
We are not human in their eyes.

255
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,820
They look at me and see a weapon.

256
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,880
They look at her and see a whore.

257
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:28,030
They look at me and they see a misshapen little beast.

258
00:19:28,070 --> 00:19:30,260
Their contempt is their weakness.

259
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,890
They'll underestimate us every time

260
00:19:31,890 --> 00:19:34,010
and we will use that to our advantage.

261
00:19:34,530 --> 00:19:36,130
You will not use them.

262
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:39,510
They will use you. That is what they do.

263
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:01,840
You all right?

264
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:04,560
Why don't you sit and catch your breath?

265
00:20:05,850 --> 00:20:07,000
I'm fine.

266
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:10,730
I don't think you could ride the dragon.

267
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,600
20 years ago, maybe.

268
00:20:13,550 --> 00:20:15,650
- What? - Our queen.

269
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:19,310
She's wild, you know. Don't let her size fool you.

270
00:20:19,570 --> 00:20:21,780
It's hard enough for me and I'm a young man.

271
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,900
You, I don't think your heart could take it.

272
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:32,090
Must make you angry that our queen chose me.

273
00:20:32,090 --> 00:20:35,230
Makes me sad. You'll disappoint her before long.

274
00:20:35,230 --> 00:20:36,300
She'll move on.

275
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:37,970
We'll all disappoint her before long.

276
00:20:37,970 --> 00:20:39,540
We need each other right now.

277
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:40,950
After we're done needing each other...

278
00:20:40,950 --> 00:20:44,190
Oh, I don't want to fight you, Jorah the Andal.

279
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,840
What do I have to gain?

280
00:20:45,970 --> 00:20:48,860
If I win, I'm the shit who killed an old man.

281
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:51,650
If I lose, I'm the shit who was killed by an old man.

282
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:56,550
You didn't get much discipline as a child, did you?

283
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,700
None.

284
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,540
The road running through the Horse Gate,

285
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:09,230
they call that the godsway.

286
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,950
Eastern Market, Western Market.

287
00:21:12,570 --> 00:21:13,840
When Khal Drogo died,

288
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:16,560
she was supposed to come here and join the Dosh Khaleen,

289
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:18,420
the widows of the dead khals.

290
00:21:19,970 --> 00:21:21,670
That's where they would have taken her,

291
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:24,290
the Temple of the Dosh Khaleen.

292
00:21:33,890 --> 00:21:34,960
What are you doing?

293
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:37,570
It's forbidden to carry weapons in the sacred city.

294
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:38,980
Isn't it forbidden to sneak

295
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,900
into their city and steal their khaleesi?

296
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,910
If they spot us and we're unarmed,

297
00:21:42,910 --> 00:21:45,350
we'll say we're traders heading for the Western Market.

298
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:47,160
But if they see weapons...

299
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:49,270
You're asking a dog to hand over his teeth.

300
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:51,290
There's 100,000 of them down there.

301
00:21:51,290 --> 00:21:52,780
We can't fight our way out.

302
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:55,520
We wait till dark, and then we'll find her.

303
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:08,660
I'm very attached to this knife.

304
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:22,130
Don't worry. It didn't touch you.

305
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,000
You know what happens?

306
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:26,890
I know what happens.

307
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,350
I'll do it myself.

308
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,390
I should have been born a Dothraki.

309
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:34,890
Come on.

310
00:24:54,550 --> 00:24:57,700
Told you, I'm very attached to this knife.

311
00:24:58,770 --> 00:24:59,880
You all right?

312
00:25:00,770 --> 00:25:02,850
If they find a body with a stab wound,

313
00:25:02,850 --> 00:25:04,840
the whole city will be looking for us.

314
00:27:15,810 --> 00:27:17,980
- No, don't hurt her. - She'll give us away.

315
00:27:17,980 --> 00:27:19,520
We have to go now.

316
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:27,210
We will never get out of Vaes Dothrak alive.

317
00:27:27,210 --> 00:27:28,890
All we can do is try.

318
00:27:30,130 --> 00:27:31,090
No.

319
00:27:32,390 --> 00:27:34,050
We can do more than that.

320
00:27:34,330 --> 00:27:35,980
And you're going to help me.

321
00:28:45,650 --> 00:28:49,610
If I were to let you leave right now, where would you go?

322
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,660
What would you seek out?

323
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:55,530
I'd go to my brother,

324
00:28:56,290 --> 00:28:58,090
my husband, my family.

325
00:28:58,090 --> 00:29:02,050
Of course, but for you, that means seeking out money,

326
00:29:02,050 --> 00:29:04,260
finery, power.

327
00:29:05,140 --> 00:29:08,280
Seeking out your family means seeking out sin.

328
00:29:09,130 --> 00:29:11,370
I'm not maligning you.

329
00:29:11,370 --> 00:29:13,490
I sought those things out, too.

330
00:29:14,140 --> 00:29:16,490
To the exclusion of all else.

331
00:29:18,210 --> 00:29:19,960
My father was a cobbler.

332
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:23,250
He died when I was young and I took over his shop.

333
00:29:24,390 --> 00:29:26,870
He was a simple man and he made simple shoes.

334
00:29:26,870 --> 00:29:30,450
But I found that the more work I put into my shoes,

335
00:29:30,450 --> 00:29:32,180
the more people wanted them.

336
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:34,840
Fine leather, ornamentation,

337
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:37,950
detailing, and time.

338
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,490
Time most of all.

339
00:29:40,490 --> 00:29:43,260
Dozens of hours spent on a single pair.

340
00:29:43,300 --> 00:29:45,010
Quality takes time.

341
00:29:45,010 --> 00:29:46,320
Yes.

342
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:49,290
I imagine you've worn a year

343
00:29:49,290 --> 00:29:51,500
of someone's life on your back.

344
00:29:52,380 --> 00:29:55,280
The highborn liked to cover their feet with my time

345
00:29:55,290 --> 00:29:57,310
and they paid well for the privilege.

346
00:29:58,280 --> 00:29:59,550
I used their money

347
00:29:59,550 --> 00:30:02,430
to buy a taste of their lives for myself.

348
00:30:03,430 --> 00:30:04,940
Each time I indulged,

349
00:30:04,940 --> 00:30:09,010
I felt myself ascending to something better.

350
00:30:09,010 --> 00:30:11,030
And one day you walked through a graveyard

351
00:30:11,030 --> 00:30:12,820
and realized it was all for nothing

352
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:15,370
and set out on the path to righteousness.

353
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:18,140
Book of the Stranger, verse 25.

354
00:30:18,910 --> 00:30:20,760
You know "The Seven-Pointed Star."

355
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:23,870
Septa Unella reads it to me. At me.

356
00:30:24,020 --> 00:30:27,790
Yes, yes, she does enjoy reading at people.

357
00:30:29,540 --> 00:30:30,850
You're close.

358
00:30:31,530 --> 00:30:33,530
But it wasn't a graveyard.

359
00:30:34,060 --> 00:30:35,650
It was a feast.

360
00:30:35,730 --> 00:30:37,710
I bought old fine wine

361
00:30:38,130 --> 00:30:39,970
and young pretty girls

362
00:30:40,330 --> 00:30:43,160
and invited my friends to come and share it all.

363
00:30:44,130 --> 00:30:47,190
We passed around the wine, passed around the women,

364
00:30:47,570 --> 00:30:50,140
and soon we fell into a stupor.

365
00:30:53,610 --> 00:30:55,450
I woke before dawn.

366
00:30:56,470 --> 00:30:58,360
I could barely stand.

367
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:03,510
Everyone else was asleep on the couches or on the floor,

368
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:08,730
lying in heaps next to their fine clothes.

369
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:11,620
The truth of their bodies laid bare.

370
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:15,490
I could smell them

371
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:19,510
beneath the incense and the perfume

372
00:31:20,470 --> 00:31:23,930
and the fine food that had already started to turn.

373
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:28,610
And I saw it with perfect clarity.

374
00:31:30,410 --> 00:31:32,470
I saw what my sins were.

375
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:37,140
The gold I had, the wine I drank, the women I used,

376
00:31:37,150 --> 00:31:41,220
my ceaseless struggle to maintain my position.

377
00:31:45,990 --> 00:31:48,000
It was all part of a story.

378
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:53,870
A story I was telling myself about who I was.

379
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:56,340
A collection of lies

380
00:31:56,340 --> 00:31:58,380
that would disappear in the light.

381
00:31:58,740 --> 00:32:01,450
The people I was trying to climb away from,

382
00:32:02,630 --> 00:32:04,110
the beggars in the street,

383
00:32:04,110 --> 00:32:05,390
the poor,

384
00:32:05,690 --> 00:32:08,510
they were closer to the truth than I ever was.

385
00:32:09,390 --> 00:32:11,110
So what did you do?

386
00:32:12,140 --> 00:32:14,090
I left to go and find them.

387
00:32:14,090 --> 00:32:16,950
I didn't even put on my shoes.

388
00:32:17,910 --> 00:32:21,440
I walked out the door and never went back.

389
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:29,630
Come, let's go and see him.

390
00:32:30,480 --> 00:32:32,370
- Who? - Your brother.

391
00:32:49,330 --> 00:32:50,510
Loras.

392
00:32:57,050 --> 00:32:58,390
Loras.

393
00:33:17,690 --> 00:33:19,050
Listen to me.

394
00:33:19,260 --> 00:33:21,630
You need to stay strong.

395
00:33:25,250 --> 00:33:26,990
I can't stay strong.

396
00:33:28,140 --> 00:33:29,350
I never was strong.

397
00:33:29,350 --> 00:33:30,780
You are strong.

398
00:33:31,220 --> 00:33:33,850
You are the future of our house,

399
00:33:33,860 --> 00:33:35,270
the future of our family.

400
00:33:35,270 --> 00:33:37,050
I don't care about that.

401
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:42,110
Have you... have you told them that?

402
00:33:42,110 --> 00:33:43,620
That you don't care?

403
00:33:44,890 --> 00:33:47,840
I just want it to stop.

404
00:33:50,280 --> 00:33:51,560
Help me.

405
00:33:58,570 --> 00:34:01,250
They want me to help you.

406
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:04,960
They want me to help tear you down.

407
00:34:05,570 --> 00:34:08,600
That's why he's letting me see you. I know it is.

408
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:12,350
And if either of us give in to what they want, then they win.

409
00:34:12,350 --> 00:34:14,120
Let them win.

410
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:17,150
Just make it stop.

411
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:19,720
Please.

412
00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:23,380
All right.

413
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:31,660
And now, how to avert disaster with our current predicament.

414
00:34:31,660 --> 00:34:33,670
This High Sparrow.

415
00:34:33,950 --> 00:34:37,110
I have dealt with fanatics of every description, Your Grace.

416
00:34:37,130 --> 00:34:40,650
Not setting them off, that's the most important thing.

417
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:44,180
You are beset with enemies both within and without.

418
00:34:44,180 --> 00:34:45,660
What are you doing here?

419
00:34:48,620 --> 00:34:52,210
I am advising the king on our current predicament.

420
00:34:52,210 --> 00:34:55,300
- Leave. - I am a member of the small council.

421
00:34:56,340 --> 00:34:57,160
The king...

422
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:59,380
Is this a small council meeting?

423
00:34:59,380 --> 00:35:00,700
Obviously not.

424
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:04,160
I'm here to lend my wisdom and my support.

425
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:07,200
Thank you for your counsel, Grand Maester.

426
00:35:07,450 --> 00:35:09,170
That will be all for now.

427
00:35:09,830 --> 00:35:11,200
Your Grace.

428
00:35:35,210 --> 00:35:38,490
Since I've missed the past several small council meetings,

429
00:35:39,020 --> 00:35:41,190
I wanted to speak to you about a few things.

430
00:35:43,180 --> 00:35:45,190
I've been thinking about the High Sparrow.

431
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:47,460
As have we all, unfortunately.

432
00:35:48,340 --> 00:35:50,980
We need to be careful in dealing with such a man.

433
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:54,960
To prevent things from escalating any further.

434
00:35:57,220 --> 00:35:59,460
We have to be careful not to antagonize him.

435
00:35:59,460 --> 00:36:01,980
He has Margaery. We can't put her at risk.

436
00:36:01,980 --> 00:36:03,820
- He's dangerous. - Look at me.

437
00:36:04,730 --> 00:36:06,390
What did they do to me?

438
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:08,620
To the king's own mother?

439
00:36:13,420 --> 00:36:14,890
It's all right.

440
00:36:16,250 --> 00:36:18,210
It's done. It's in the past.

441
00:36:19,050 --> 00:36:20,430
And of course

442
00:36:20,860 --> 00:36:23,120
Margaery's safety is paramount.

443
00:36:25,010 --> 00:36:28,810
You don't like Margaery, do you?

444
00:36:30,690 --> 00:36:33,780
Whether I like her or not is completely unimportant.

445
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:37,840
Margaery is the queen.

446
00:36:39,340 --> 00:36:42,620
Queens must command respect. Kings even more so.

447
00:36:42,620 --> 00:36:45,350
Not just for their own sake, but for everyone's.

448
00:36:47,430 --> 00:36:50,610
The High Sparrow has no respect for kings or queens.

449
00:36:51,140 --> 00:36:53,160
No respect for anything in this world.

450
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:55,690
He has no use for the things of this world.

451
00:36:55,690 --> 00:36:58,930
He wants to knock them down and replace them with what?

452
00:36:59,660 --> 00:37:01,490
With fantasies.

453
00:37:01,810 --> 00:37:03,590
With beggars in the street.

454
00:37:03,590 --> 00:37:04,860
With nothing.

455
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:08,060
Mother...

456
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:12,180
there's something I want to tell you.

457
00:37:13,260 --> 00:37:15,250
Something the High Sparrow told me.

458
00:37:18,650 --> 00:37:20,240
You've spoken with him?

459
00:37:22,020 --> 00:37:25,050
I promised him I wouldn't tell anyone.

460
00:37:25,050 --> 00:37:26,420
If he found out I told...

461
00:37:26,420 --> 00:37:27,550
It would be a breach of confidence

462
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:28,740
which he would not take lightly

463
00:37:28,740 --> 00:37:31,150
given his constant prattling about the truth.

464
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:36,590
I am your mother.

465
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,730
You can always trust me.

466
00:37:48,420 --> 00:37:49,510
The small council meeting

467
00:37:49,510 --> 00:37:51,740
has been postponed on the king's orders.

468
00:37:51,740 --> 00:37:54,340
I would have thought we were perfectly clear the first time.

469
00:37:54,340 --> 00:37:55,540
You're not welcome.

470
00:37:55,540 --> 00:37:57,250
You once spoke of your respect for our father

471
00:37:57,250 --> 00:38:00,050
because he understood the necessity of working with one's rivals.

472
00:38:00,050 --> 00:38:04,880
My dear, you have been stripped of your dignity and authority,

473
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:08,180
publically shamed, and confined to the Red Keep.

474
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:10,440
What's left to work with?

475
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:12,230
Cersei is the mother of the king.

476
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,960
She has the king's ear and his trust.

477
00:38:15,800 --> 00:38:17,720
And the king has been speaking regularly

478
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:20,970
with the High Sparrow about Queen Margaery and Ser Loras.

479
00:38:21,370 --> 00:38:23,580
The High Sparrow seized power knowing full well

480
00:38:23,580 --> 00:38:26,420
we'd bicker amongst ourselves instead of seizing it back.

481
00:38:26,630 --> 00:38:28,910
Here we are. Well done to us.

482
00:38:29,230 --> 00:38:30,640
Now the future of the Seven Kingdoms

483
00:38:30,650 --> 00:38:33,100
rests in his dirty peasant hands.

484
00:38:33,100 --> 00:38:35,270
In a few days, he'll have a trial for me.

485
00:38:35,950 --> 00:38:39,370
But before that, Queen Margaery will make her walk of atonement.

486
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:43,070
Yes, Margaery will repent her sins

487
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:45,200
before the good people of the city.

488
00:38:45,750 --> 00:38:46,680
Oh, no.

489
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:49,590
That cannot happen.

490
00:38:50,930 --> 00:38:52,520
That will not happen.

491
00:38:52,710 --> 00:38:53,780
I agree.

492
00:38:57,130 --> 00:38:59,730
You've got the second largest army in Westeros.

493
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:01,430
You'll bring them into the city,

494
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:04,180
stop Queen Margaery's humiliation before it starts,

495
00:39:04,180 --> 00:39:06,170
and take her back into Crown custody.

496
00:39:06,930 --> 00:39:08,300
The king has ordered me

497
00:39:08,300 --> 00:39:10,630
to take no action against the High Sparrow

498
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,780
or the Faith Militant out of fear for the queen's safety.

499
00:39:13,790 --> 00:39:15,530
You will take no action at all.

500
00:39:15,750 --> 00:39:18,400
When the Tyrell armies come, you will stand down.

501
00:39:19,370 --> 00:39:21,760
Are you expressly forbidden from standing down?

502
00:39:22,470 --> 00:39:25,220
No, but if the king should call...

503
00:39:25,220 --> 00:39:26,020
The whole thing will be over

504
00:39:26,020 --> 00:39:28,220
before anyone can call on you to do anything.

505
00:39:28,220 --> 00:39:31,810
When the High Sparrow is in custody or dead, preferably,

506
00:39:31,970 --> 00:39:34,410
and Margaery's back at Tommen's side,

507
00:39:34,820 --> 00:39:37,320
do you think the king will be angry at the outcome?

508
00:39:37,400 --> 00:39:39,990
You hate these fanatics as much as we do.

509
00:39:40,660 --> 00:39:42,940
You hate what they've done to your son.

510
00:39:43,170 --> 00:39:44,950
Do you want Lancel back?

511
00:39:45,180 --> 00:39:46,980
Or have you given him up for good?

512
00:39:49,270 --> 00:39:50,860
Of course I want him back.

513
00:39:54,500 --> 00:39:55,850
Then stand aside

514
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:59,200
and let the people that took him from you be destroyed.

515
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:04,490
If it doesn't go as planned,

516
00:40:04,920 --> 00:40:07,340
the sparrows have many friends in this city.

517
00:40:07,650 --> 00:40:09,890
We'll have civil war. Many will die.

518
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:12,660
Many will die no matter what we do.

519
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,830
Better them than us.

520
00:41:12,890 --> 00:41:15,270
They told me you were home and I didn't believe it.

521
00:41:16,990 --> 00:41:19,140
"Theon Greyjoy?" I said.

522
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:21,100
"He's dead.

523
00:41:22,510 --> 00:41:24,420
He's been dead a long time."

524
00:41:27,910 --> 00:41:29,020
He let you go?

525
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:31,110
I escaped.

526
00:41:33,900 --> 00:41:35,180
I can't hear you.

527
00:41:35,810 --> 00:41:37,080
I escaped.

528
00:41:40,140 --> 00:41:41,180
Look at me.

529
00:41:50,580 --> 00:41:51,730
Look at me!

530
00:41:52,860 --> 00:41:55,310
Men died trying to rescue you.

531
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:56,680
Good men.

532
00:41:57,870 --> 00:41:59,020
My men.

533
00:42:00,450 --> 00:42:01,550
I'm sorry.

534
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:03,850
You were my brother.

535
00:42:04,760 --> 00:42:07,300
You were a spoiled little cunt, but you were my brother

536
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:09,430
and I risked everything for you

537
00:42:10,140 --> 00:42:11,040
and you betrayed me.

538
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:13,140
I know. I know and I'm sorry.

539
00:42:13,140 --> 00:42:14,430
Stop saying that.

540
00:42:15,430 --> 00:42:16,460
He broke me.

541
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:19,570
He broke me into 1,000 pieces.

542
00:42:19,580 --> 00:42:20,900
- I know. - You don't know.

543
00:42:20,900 --> 00:42:23,110
He sent us one of those pieces.

544
00:42:23,830 --> 00:42:25,520
That's why I came for you.

545
00:42:31,770 --> 00:42:33,360
Why did you come here?

546
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:35,490
Where else could I go?

547
00:42:35,490 --> 00:42:38,460
You heard Father was dead and you thought you'd claim the crown?

548
00:42:39,350 --> 00:42:41,690
No, no. I only heard he died after we docked.

549
00:42:41,690 --> 00:42:44,220
You happen to show up on Pyke right before the kingsmoot?

550
00:42:44,220 --> 00:42:45,140
I didn't know.

551
00:42:48,850 --> 00:42:51,940
You think any ironborn wants you to be king

552
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:53,690
after what you've done?

553
00:42:54,010 --> 00:42:55,550
I don't want to be king.

554
00:42:56,250 --> 00:42:57,600
What do you want?

555
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:01,410
I should have listened to you. You're the only one...

556
00:43:01,410 --> 00:43:03,820
That doesn't matter anymore. Stop crying.

557
00:43:03,890 --> 00:43:05,000
Look at me.

558
00:43:07,310 --> 00:43:09,280
Tell me what you want.

559
00:43:13,920 --> 00:43:15,940
You should rule the Iron Islands.

560
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:19,040
Let me help you.

561
00:43:46,520 --> 00:43:48,160
They've cleaned you up nicely.

562
00:43:50,660 --> 00:43:51,790
You know who I am?

563
00:43:54,040 --> 00:43:55,150
A lord.

564
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:56,160
Yes.

565
00:43:57,360 --> 00:43:58,540
A lord.

566
00:44:00,280 --> 00:44:02,120
You've seen my banners?

567
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:04,560
The flayed man.

568
00:44:05,670 --> 00:44:07,300
Does that worry you at all?

569
00:44:09,010 --> 00:44:10,260
You eat them after?

570
00:44:14,400 --> 00:44:15,230
No.

571
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:17,660
Then I've seen worse.

572
00:44:42,530 --> 00:44:44,010
You served the Starks?

573
00:44:44,320 --> 00:44:46,740
Aye. They put me in chains

574
00:44:46,740 --> 00:44:48,750
and put a sword at my throat,

575
00:44:48,870 --> 00:44:50,390
so I served them.

576
00:44:50,450 --> 00:44:52,950
The Starks have been gone for a long time,

577
00:44:53,930 --> 00:44:56,440
but you kept protecting Rickon.

578
00:44:56,770 --> 00:45:00,020
He'd fetch a good price to the right buyer.

579
00:45:00,400 --> 00:45:01,830
I served his family a long time.

580
00:45:01,830 --> 00:45:03,390
Didn't get no wages.

581
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:07,030
Way I see it, I'm owed.

582
00:45:09,730 --> 00:45:11,120
Be that as it may,

583
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:14,930
Rickon's not yours to sell anymore.

584
00:45:15,220 --> 00:45:16,180
He's mine.

585
00:45:16,710 --> 00:45:19,280
So what use could I possibly have for you?

586
00:45:22,380 --> 00:45:24,430
I can give you what you want.

587
00:45:24,560 --> 00:45:26,550
And you're sure you know what that is?

588
00:45:28,310 --> 00:45:30,630
Same thing men always want.

589
00:45:31,850 --> 00:45:36,070
And when they really want it, they give it a bath first.

590
00:45:44,470 --> 00:45:46,180
You're a good talker.

591
00:45:48,780 --> 00:45:49,880
I like that.

592
00:45:58,790 --> 00:46:01,980
You're a much better talker than Theon Greyjoy.

593
00:46:03,710 --> 00:46:04,840
That so?

594
00:46:05,430 --> 00:46:07,910
I had to work hard to get him talking.

595
00:46:08,590 --> 00:46:09,750
But he talked.

596
00:46:10,660 --> 00:46:11,790
They all do.

597
00:46:12,540 --> 00:46:14,100
He told me everything.

598
00:46:15,400 --> 00:46:18,090
All about the Stark boys,

599
00:46:18,090 --> 00:46:19,690
who helped them escape,

600
00:46:20,360 --> 00:46:22,010
and how she did it.

601
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:51,420
Open the gate!

602
00:47:39,340 --> 00:47:40,940
Sorry about the food.

603
00:47:41,730 --> 00:47:43,240
It's not what we're known for.

604
00:47:43,300 --> 00:47:45,860
That's all right. There are more important things.

605
00:47:51,190 --> 00:47:52,810
A letter for you, Lord Commander.

606
00:47:54,500 --> 00:47:56,230
I'm not Lord Commander anymore.

607
00:48:16,580 --> 00:48:18,860
"To the traitor and bastard Jon Snow.

608
00:48:19,300 --> 00:48:22,140
You allowed thousands of wildlings past the Wall.

609
00:48:22,220 --> 00:48:23,840
You have betrayed your own kind.

610
00:48:23,840 --> 00:48:25,510
You have betrayed the North.

611
00:48:25,970 --> 00:48:29,210
Winterfell is mine, bastard. Come and see.

612
00:48:30,530 --> 00:48:32,830
Your brother Rickon is in my dungeon.

613
00:48:41,540 --> 00:48:43,430
His direwolf's skin is on my floor.

614
00:48:43,430 --> 00:48:46,430
Come and see. I want my bride back.

615
00:48:46,430 --> 00:48:47,590
Send her to me, bastard,

616
00:48:47,590 --> 00:48:50,180
and I will not trouble you or your wildling lovers.

617
00:48:50,380 --> 00:48:52,940
Keep her from me and I will ride north and slaughter

618
00:48:52,940 --> 00:48:56,460
every wildling man, woman, and babe living under your protection.

619
00:48:57,120 --> 00:48:59,960
You will watch as I skin them living. You... "

620
00:49:02,600 --> 00:49:03,420
Go on.

621
00:49:04,460 --> 00:49:05,750
It's just more of the same.

622
00:49:10,990 --> 00:49:14,630
"You will watch as my soldiers take turns raping your sister.

623
00:49:15,980 --> 00:49:17,140
You will watch as my dogs

624
00:49:17,140 --> 00:49:19,360
devour your wild little brother.

625
00:49:21,980 --> 00:49:23,330
Then I will spoon your eyes

626
00:49:23,330 --> 00:49:25,800
from their sockets and let my dogs do the rest.

627
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:29,400
Come and see. Ramsay Bolton, Lord of Winterfell

628
00:49:29,850 --> 00:49:31,340
and Warden of the North."

629
00:49:35,110 --> 00:49:38,810
Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the North.

630
00:49:39,090 --> 00:49:40,310
His father's dead.

631
00:49:42,510 --> 00:49:43,790
Ramsay killed him.

632
00:49:43,970 --> 00:49:45,690
- And now he has Rickon. - We don't know that.

633
00:49:45,690 --> 00:49:46,690
Yes, we do.

634
00:49:48,610 --> 00:49:51,110
How many men does he have in his army?

635
00:49:53,210 --> 00:49:54,830
I heard him say 5,000 once

636
00:49:54,830 --> 00:49:57,170
when he was talking about Stannis's attack.

637
00:49:57,970 --> 00:49:59,260
How many do you have?

638
00:49:59,260 --> 00:50:00,970
That can march and fight?

639
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:04,220
2,000.

640
00:50:05,540 --> 00:50:08,170
The rest are children and old people.

641
00:50:13,190 --> 00:50:15,990
You're the son of the last true Warden of the North.

642
00:50:16,170 --> 00:50:17,740
Northern families are loyal.

643
00:50:17,740 --> 00:50:19,460
They'll fight for you if you ask.

644
00:50:21,620 --> 00:50:26,060
A monster has taken our home and our brother.

645
00:50:27,260 --> 00:50:30,140
We have to go back to Winterfell and save them both.

